<DocsPageSectionTitle>
    Best Practices
</DocsPageSectionTitle>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Support Precise Choices
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Use a clear label and show the resulting color value when precision or reuse matters. Offer a sensible initial color and, when appropriate, a way to return to the product default.
</DocsPageParagraph>

<DocsPageSubsectionTitle IncludeInToc="false">
    Color Contrast
</DocsPageSubsectionTitle>

<DocsPageParagraph>
    Validate the contrast of user-selected foreground and background colors before applying them to text or controls. When the full picker interface is unnecessary, use the more compact <Anchor To="docs/components/color-input">ColorInput</Anchor> component.
</DocsPageParagraph>

